{"File":"/home/prem/Projects/Flightreader/SPECS.md","LineNumber":1161,"LineContent":"DJI aircraft flight controllers execute real-time RTOS firmware (typically based on VxWorks or FreeRTOS) that continuously serializes internal bus messages to onboard flash memory. These files bear the `.DAT` extension."}
{"File":"/home/prem/Projects/Flightreader/SPECS.md","LineNumber":1165,"LineContent":"Every message frame in a `.DAT` file adheres to a standardized framing structure:"}
{"File":"/home/prem/Projects/Flightreader/SPECS.md","LineNumber":1204,"LineContent":"To synchronize a 10 Hz mobile `.txt` log with a 100 Hz aircraft `.DAT` blackbox log:"}
{"File":"/home/prem/Projects/Flightreader/SPECS.md","LineNumber":1206,"LineContent":"1. Extract `HomeDataRecorderFileIndex` from `.txt` Home Record (ID 2). Locate matching `FLY{index}.DAT`."}
{"File":"/home/prem/Projects/Flightreader/SPECS.md","LineNumber":1208,"LineContent":"3. In `.DAT`, scan Payload `0x12` (Motor) for the timestamp where rotor RPM transitions from 0 to idle speed (\u003e 1,200 RPM)."}
